---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import GradientText from "../../components/GradientText.astro";
import PlayableNav from "../../components/PlayableNav.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Playable Release Quality & Platform Readiness | Aniloom Technologies" description="A bounded playable-ad review package covering critical journey, responsive states, agreed variants, platform constraints, corrections, retest, and release disposition.">
  <main id="main-content">
    <PlayableNav />
    <section class="page-hero page-hero--service section-shell">
      <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal>Release Quality & Platform Readiness</p>
      <h1 data-reveal>A bounded review before the next <GradientText>release decision.</GradientText></h1>
      <p class="page-hero__lead" data-reveal>For teams with an existing playable that needs structured review across its critical journey, responsive states, agreed variants, and known target-environment constraints.</p>
      <div class="page-hero__actions" data-reveal><button class="button" type="button" data-contact-open>Discuss the package</button><a class="text-link" href="#package">See the package <span>↓</span></a></div>
    </section>

    <section class="entry-points section-shell section-pad" id="package">
      <div class="section-heading" data-reveal><div><p class="eyebrow">Good fit</p><h2>Use it when release questions are still scattered.</h2></div><p>The package creates a common view of what matters, what was reviewed, what changed, and what still requires acceptance or action.</p></div>
      <div class="entry-grid">
        <article data-reveal><span>01</span><h2>Before delivery</h2><p>A playable is approaching handoff, but critical flows, responsive states, or target constraints have not been reviewed together.</p></article>
        <article data-reveal><span>02</span><h2>After adaptation</h2><p>New creative, localization, orientation, links, end cards, integrations, or variants may have changed the risk profile.</p></article>
        <article data-reveal><span>03</span><h2>After correction</h2><p>The team needs retest evidence and a concise disposition instead of a loose collection of screenshots and messages.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="system-band section-pad">
      <div class="section-shell">
        <div class="section-heading" data-reveal><div><p class="eyebrow">Package structure</p><h2>From scoped intake to documented disposition.</h2></div><p>Final depth, schedule, review rounds, devices, browsers, orientations, variants, and target environments are agreed before work begins.</p></div>
        <ol class="package-steps">
          <li data-reveal><span>01</span><div><h3>Scope and risk map</h3><p>Confirm inputs, decision, critical journey, acceptance criteria, meaningful states, configurations, and evidence format.</p></div></li>
          <li data-reveal><span>02</span><div><h3>Structured review</h3><p>Exercise the agreed journey and states across responsive orientations, variants, and known platform constraints.</p></div></li>
          <li data-reveal><span>03</span><div><h3>Issue triage and correction</h3><p>Record actionable findings, align ownership, and coordinate engineering corrections or saved layout changes where included.</p></div></li>
          <li data-reveal><span>04</span><div><h3>Retest and disposition</h3><p>Recheck corrected and related states, then document reviewed scope, remaining risk, blocked areas, and the release decision still required.</p></div></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="deliverable section-shell section-pad">
      <div class="section-heading" data-reveal><div><p class="eyebrow">Typical outputs</p><h2>Evidence the team can keep using.</h2></div><p>Names and formats are adapted to the working environment. The package does not create external certification or replace platform review.</p></div>
      <div class="deliverable-grid">
        <div data-reveal><span>Scope and configuration matrix</span><p>Agreed journey, states, orientations, variants, platforms, assumptions, dependencies, and exclusions.</p></div>
        <div data-reveal><span>Findings and evidence</span><p>Prioritized issue record with reproduction context, visual evidence, expected behavior, and current ownership.</p></div>
        <div data-reveal><span>Correction record</span><p>Changes made or requested, affected states, related regression checks, and retest status.</p></div>
        <div data-reveal><span>Release disposition</span><p>Reviewed scope, passed areas, open defects, blocked checks, accepted limitations, owners, and next decision.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="boundary-band section-shell" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">Important boundary</p>
      <h2>Readiness evidence is not a guarantee.</h2>
      <p>Aniloom does not present this package as certification, defect-free assurance, campaign-performance proof, or a guarantee that an advertising platform will accept a build. Platform rules and external review outcomes remain outside Aniloom’s control.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="callout section-shell section-pad" data-reveal><p class="eyebrow">Scope the decision</p><h2>Bring the playable, target list, and deadline.</h2><p>We will confirm whether this bounded package fits or whether development work, broader Quality Engineering, or a different review boundary is more useful.</p><div class="callout__actions"><a class="text-link" href="/playable-ads/qa-release-readiness/">Explore the QA approach <span>↗</span></a><button class="button" type="button" data-contact-open>Discuss the package</button></div></section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
